<article class="env-lemma" id="0E9T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E9T">Lemma <span data-tag="0E9T">48.17.10</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F42" data-tag="0F42">48.16.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of $\textit{FTS}_ S$. If $f$ is flat, then $f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y$ is a $Y$-perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $\mathcal{O}_ X \to R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y, f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Both assertions are local on $X$. Thus we may assume $X$ and $Y$ are affine. Then Remark <a href="/tag/0BV2" data-tag="0BV2">48.17.5</a> turns the lemma into an algebra lemma, namely Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BZW" data-tag="0BZW">47.25.2</a>. (Use Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DI2" data-tag="0DI2">36.35.3</a> to match the languages.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>